[COMMENTS]
STATION,Velocity area station on the River Girvan. Flows affected by abstractions from Loch Bradan. GENERAL: Velocity area station approx. 15m wide. STATION HYDROMETRY: Low flow control is an informal gravel weir built in 1982, which is subject to re-grading in substantial floods. Flood banks contain all flows (pre-1982, right bank inundated beyond 2.2m). Peak flow ratings from current meter gaugings. Rating for period up to 1982 max gauging 2.2m (about 0.9 QMED); post-1982 max gauging up to 1.9m (about 0.7 QMED), simple extrapolation beyond. Gaugings to 1982 show scatter; may suggest a changing relationship. FLOW RECORD: Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2022 (WINFAP Files v11). FLOW REGIME: Runoff diminished by abstractions from Loch Bradan. Additional storage in a few high level lochs.
CATCHMENT,Upland catchment draining from Carrick Forest. Complex geology: Ordovician/Carboniferous metamorphics and igneous formations; predominantly overlain by superficial deposits, drift and peat also. Mostly hill pasture with some mixed farming in the valley and afforestation in the headwaters; several lochs.
Qmed Suitability,Gauged to near QMED.
Pooling Suitability,Only after June 1982 when an embankment was built to allow for containment of flows above 2.2m.
[END]
